        "The lesson is to look for a gap between:\n- A cheap manual product\n- A premium professional product\nPotential questions:\n- Is the expensive product genuinely overbuilt for some users?\n- Is there a group that needs the function but not every premium feature?\n- Can a simpler design deliver the core benefit safely?\n- Is the price gap large enough to support a viable product?\n- Is the existing premium product expensive because of low volume, regulation, or technical difficulty?\nDo not assume that a high price and a poor website mean an easy opportunity. The high price may reflect difficult engineering, low-volume manufacturing, service requirements, or certification."
