        "The broader pattern:\n1. Find a product category where many options feel generic.\n2. Identify a specific customer group.\n3. Learn what that group values.\n4. Improve the product around those values.\n5. Build a recognizable brand and customer experience.\n6. Price according to the value delivered.\nPremium does not simply mean expensive. It must mean meaningfully better for the intended buyer.\nQuestions for a premium repositioning\n- Who uses this product frequently?\n- What do they dislike about existing options?\n- Which details matter most to them?\n- Do they care about comfort, design, fit, durability, or status?\n- Are they willing to pay more?\n- Can you reach them efficiently?\n- Can you deliver consistent quality?"
